+From 2befccf0decabd5f2187ce69e87221f9665a86fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: lestephen <30328443+lestephen@users.noreply.github.com>
+Date: Sun, 17 May 2026 08:24:05 -0700
+Subject: [PATCH 26/26] feat(critique): skill-critique + /octo:critique for
+ adversarial multi-LLM review of arbitrary scope
+MIME-Version: 1.0
+Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
+Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit
+
+The existing review skills covered specific cases but left a gap:
+
+  /octo:review              — code defect / security / perf focused
+  /octo:argument-strength   — prose-only argument structure
+  /octo:debate              — picks between N pre-specified options
+  /octo:defensibility-pass  — external-send hostile-review gate (3-pass)
+
+Open-ended "I made this choice / built this thing — would a hostile
+expert tear it apart?" had no home. Users hit it with technology
+choices, architecture proposals, ADRs, RFCs, general approaches.
+
+skill-critique fills the gap. Uses skill-lib-multi-review-doc as the
+multi-LLM dispatcher; picks adversarial angles per scope type:
+
+  code-change         technical / architectural / maintainability
+  design-doc          conceptual / alternatives-rejected / operational
+  technology-choice   cost / fit + exit cost / alternatives
+  approach            assumption-challenge / what-if-X / simplest-alt
+  architecture        coupling / failure modes / 2-year evolution
+  decision            reversibility / evidence quality / dissent
+  prose               refuse and route to /octo:argument-strength
+
+Each provider attacks from one angle; synthesis surfaces objections by
+severity × confidence (objections raised by 2+ providers get higher
+weight than single-provider HIGHs). Output verdicts:
+  STRONG | DEFENSIBLE WITH FIXES | LOAD-BEARING WEAKNESSES | NEEDS REDESIGN
+
+/octo:critique slash command routes to the skill with the standard
+MANDATORY COMPLIANCE / EXECUTION MECHANISM framing.
+
+Manifest updates: 51 -> 52 commands, 58 -> 59 skills across 6 user-
+facing strings. Bump to 9.38.0-lestephen.18.
+
