++Subject: [PATCH 25/25] fix(debate): bash subcommand actually dispatches via
++ grapple_debate; removes dead submodule check
++
++bash orchestrate.sh debate "..." had been erroring with:
++
++  ERROR: AI Debate Hub not found. Please initialize the submodule:
++    git submodule update --init --recursive
++
++even though no submodule exists in the fork (.gitmodules absent;
++.dependencies/claude-skills/ absent). The submodule was the v7.4
++integration with wolverin0/claude-skills that has been superseded by
++the in-tree skill-debate skill (for the slash command path) and
++lib/debate.sh::grapple_debate (for the bash subcommand path), but the
++case branch in orchestrate.sh was never updated.
++
++The branch kept the submodule guard, kept the "AI Debate Hub by
++wolverin0" informational text, and never called any debate dispatcher.
++
++Discovery: real cfd-report-automation session (2026-05-17) where Claude
++backgrounded a debate against a consensus B+D hybrid via
++  bash orchestrate.sh -t 600 debate "Adversarial stress-test..."
++The submodule check fired and the debate never ran.
++
++This fix:
++- Replaces the case branch with a real dispatcher mirroring orchestrate.sh grapple
++- Sources lib/debate.sh, parses -r/--rounds, --principles, --mode flags
++- Calls grapple_debate (the working in-tree multi-LLM debate dispatcher)
++- Adds a real --help block and helpful no-args error
++- debate, deliberate, consensus are now functional aliases of grapple
++
++The /octo:debate slash command path (routes to skill-debate, not the
++bash subcommand) was already working and is unchanged.
++
++Bump to 9.38.0-lestephen.17.
++
