++++Subject: [PATCH 23/23] feat(provider): persistent enable/disable controls with
++++ project + user scope, env override, doctor surface, /provider command
++++MIME-Version: 1.0
++++Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
++++Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit
++++
++++The fork previously had a single provider-filter mechanism — the
++++session-scoped OCTO_ALLOWED_PROVIDERS env var (allowlist). To disable
++++one provider (e.g., "skip Copilot"), users had to list every OTHER
++++provider explicitly, which breaks when new providers are added upstream.
++++The mechanism was also undocumented and not surfaced in /octo:doctor.
++++
++++This commit adds three composable provider-control mechanisms (A+B+C),
++++all merged into a single effective deny check.
++++
++++A. Persistent denylist in providers.json
++++
++++   ~/.claude-octopus/config/providers.json  (user scope, default)
++++   ./.octopus/providers.json                (project scope)
++++
++++   {
++++     "version": "3.0",
++++     "disabled": ["copilot"]
++++   }
++++
++++B. New OCTO_DISABLED_PROVIDERS env var (session-scoped)
++++
++++   export OCTO_DISABLED_PROVIDERS=copilot,qwen
++++
++++C. UX surfacing
++++
++++   New /provider slash command:
++++     /provider list                       — status table per provider
++++     /provider disable <name> [--project] — persist a disable
++++     /provider enable <name> [--project]  — re-enable
++++     /provider status <name>              — show source of disable
++++     /provider --help                     — usage
++++
++++   /octo:doctor --verbose now shows one line per disabled provider
++++   with its source (env / project / user config).
++++
++++   README section explains all three mechanisms + precedence.
++++
++++Precedence (highest first): env > project > user.
++++A provider is OK to use iff:
++++- Not in any denylist source
++++- AND if OCTO_ALLOWED_PROVIDERS is set, in the allowlist
++++
++++Backward compatibility: OCTO_ALLOWED_PROVIDERS semantics unchanged.
++++The denylist is additive — a provider in both the allowlist AND the
++++denylist is denied (denylist trumps).
++++
++++Files:
++++- scripts/lib/provider-allowlist.sh: +89/-1 (added octo_provider_disabled,
++++  octo_disabled_set, octo_provider_disabled_source; octo_provider_allowed
++++  now consults denylist first)
++++- scripts/lib/provider-config.sh: new, +148 (mutation: enable/disable/list
++++  with idempotent jq-driven JSON manipulation, project + user scopes)
++++- scripts/orchestrate.sh: +72 (new `provider` subcommand wiring)
++++- scripts/lib/doctor.sh: +18 (per-disabled-provider info line in verbose mode)
++++- .claude/commands/provider.md: new slash command
++++- .claude-plugin/plugin.json: register provider command
++++- 5 manifest strings + README: command count 50 -> 51
++++- README: new "Enable/disable providers" section
++++
++++Bump to 9.38.0-lestephen.15.
