+++++From 4bc0a7fb974501b325aadd9bfb7999d2a528acd8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+++++From: lestephen <30328443+lestephen@users.noreply.github.com>
+++++Date: Sun, 17 May 2026 07:28:42 -0700
+++++Subject: [PATCH 22/22] fix(routing): cross-provider safety for bare-provider
+++++ routing in resolve_octopus_model
+++++
+++++Fixes #1.
+++++
+++++resolve_octopus_model had two branches for Tier 3 routing results:
+++++
+++++- Colon form ("codex:spark"): cross-provider safety check at line 130 -
+++++  added in v9.17.1 (#235 item 3) - skips the route when the prefixed
+++++  provider differs from the current resolution target.
+++++- Bare form ("perplexity"): no safety check; bare value assigned directly.
+++++
+++++When providers.json contains routing.roles.researcher = "perplexity"
+++++(bare provider name), any call resolving for a different provider got
+++++the literal string "perplexity" assigned as the model. Codex CLI was
+++++then invoked with model=perplexity, which it cannot use, producing
+++++empty output with Status: FAILED.
+++++
+++++Library-skill validation gates that check only for file existence +
+++++non-empty would see the file (it has a header) and report success
+++++while the actual dispatch had silently failed. This was the bug that
+++++made codex unusable from every library-skill multi-provider dispatch
+++++introduced in v9.38.0-lestephen.11.
+++++
+++++Fix: mirror the v9.17.1 cross-provider safety into the bare branch.
+++++
+++++- If the bare routed value matches a known provider AND differs from
+++++  the resolution target: skip the route (fall through to capability
+++++  map / default).
+++++- If the bare routed value matches a known provider AND is the same
+++++  as the resolution target: also skip (don't assign the provider name
+++++  as a literal model name) and fall through to capability/default.
+++++  Also fixes the latent issue where provider=perplexity, role=researcher
+++++  would have resolved to model=perplexity instead of model=sonar-pro.
+++++- If the bare routed value does NOT match a known provider name: treat
+++++  as literal model name (preserves existing behavior for configurations
+++++  that legitimately use bare model identifiers).
+++++
+++++Verified with three trace runs:
+++++
+++++- provider=codex, role=researcher -> resolves to gpt-5.5 (was: perplexity)
+++++- provider=perplexity, role=researcher -> resolves to sonar-pro (was: literal "perplexity")
+++++- provider=gemini, role=verifier (colon-form route) -> unchanged, gemini-3.1-pro-preview
+++++
+++++Bump to 9.38.0-lestephen.14.
