+++++++Subject: [PATCH 20/20] fix(km-lib): correct probe-single call signature and
+++++++ output file pattern in library skills
+++++++
+++++++The three library skills introduced in the previous commit (Patch #19)
+++++++documented orchestrate.sh probe-single incorrectly. Surfaced during a
+++++++2-provider smoke test before any consumer wired up to the library
+++++++skills.
+++++++
+++++++Two bugs in skill prose (no code change):
+++++++
+++++++1. Reviewer prompt was passed as $4 (original_prompt). That slot is
+++++++   metadata only - the model never sees it. The actual prompt body the
+++++++   model receives is $2 (the "perspective" slot, named historically -
+++++++   it goes through apply_persona to become the prompt).
+++++++
+++++++2. Validation gates searched for files matching
+++++++   probe-synthesis-${label}-*.md or ${label}-*.md. The actual file
+++++++   pattern written by probe_single_agent at scripts/lib/workflows.sh:128
+++++++   is <agent_type>-<task_id>.md. Validation gates would have reported
+++++++   VALIDATION FAILED for every successful dispatch.
+++++++
+++++++Fix in all three library skill prose files:
+++++++
+++++++- Restructured the dispatch code-block to pass the reviewer prompt in
+++++++  the perspective slot ($2), with a note explaining the historical
+++++++  naming.
+++++++- Restructured the validation-gate code-block to compute
+++++++  ${OUTPUT_DIR}/${agent_type}-${task_id}.md from dispatch-time state
+++++++  instead of globbing on the wrong pattern.
+++++++- Added inline comments referencing scripts/lib/workflows.sh:128 so the
+++++++  next maintainer does not repeat the misreading.
