++++++++Subject: [PATCH 19/19] feat(km): defensibility-pass + argument-strength
++++++++ skills, 3 library primitives for multi-LLM dispatch
++++++++
++++++++The existing /octo:km mode is a context-switch flag that swaps in
++++++++PRD/marketing/UX personas. That shape fits SaaS PM work but not
++++++++engineering-consulting knowledge work, which needs adversarial review
++++++++primitives: independent verification of quantitative claims,
++++++++multi-perspective red-teaming of prose arguments, and defensibility
++++++++gating before external send. This commit is Phase 1 of /octo:km making
++++++++it actually useful for that kind of work.
++++++++
++++++++Two end-user skills:
++++++++
++++++++- skill-defensibility-pass: publish-ready gate for external-bound
++++++++  documents. Three passes via library skills - (A) independent
++++++++  recompute of every quantitative claim, (B) methodology audit with
++++++++  codex + gemini reviewers, (C) internal-terms scrub + audience-tone
++++++++  lint via deterministic grep + multi-LLM review. Synthesizes
++++++++  pass/fail with what must change before send. Loads optional project
++++++++  profile YAML for banned-terms / internal-codenames / audience-tone
++++++++  rules; falls back to generic prompts when profile is absent.
++++++++
++++++++- skill-argument-strength: adversarial prose review. Three providers
++++++++  red-team a draft from different angles (technical attack, structural
++++++++  attack, audience-reception attack). Synthesis surfaces
++++++++  high-confidence objections (raised by 2+ providers) and recommends
++++++++  minimum revisions. This is /octo:debate for prose.
++++++++
++++++++Three library skills meant to be invoked from other skills/plugins:
++++++++
++++++++- skill-lib-multi-review-doc: fan a document to N providers with
++++++++  per-reviewer prompts, synthesize, return path + headline. Validation
++++++++  gate enforced. Consumer skills supply the reviewer prompts; this
++++++++  skill handles dispatch + synthesis.
++++++++
++++++++- skill-lib-multi-inspect-figure: dispatch a rendered figure to
++++++++  multiple vision-capable providers, return unified issue list. Skips
++++++++  non-vision providers. Writes inspection-log.jsonl for graduating
++++++++  recurring issue classes into deterministic lint.
++++++++
++++++++- skill-lib-independent-recompute: ask one or more providers to
++++++++  recompute a quantitative claim from source data, return verdict
++++++++  (CORROBORATED / CLAIM MATCHES SOME / CLAIM UNSUPPORTED / PROVIDERS
++++++++  DISAGREE). The last verdict is the most informative for
++++++++  defensibility work - it surfaces methodology ambiguity the document
++++++++  failed to anchor.
++++++++
++++++++All five skills follow existing octopus conventions: codex-host
++++++++adapter block, MANDATORY COMPLIANCE section, provider check via
++++++++skills/blocks/provider-check.md, visual-indicator banner, validation
++++++++gate that confirms synthesis files exist before claiming success.
++++++++
++++++++The library skills are intentionally lower-level than /octo:review or
++++++++flow-deliver. They are meant to be composed by other skills (including
++++++++third-party plugins like eki-kw, the private companion plugin being
++++++++developed in parallel). Their input contracts are explicit so
++++++++consumers can call them without re-implementing the orchestration.
++++++++
