+++++++++@@ -0,0 +1,526 @@
++++++++++From 3a8aa7f6154d332045b3d5d401721a1e872d6f28 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
++++++++++From: lestephen <30328443+lestephen@users.noreply.github.com>
++++++++++Date: Sat, 16 May 2026 15:38:58 -0700
++++++++++Subject: [PATCH 15/17] feat(tangle): checkpoint-streaming subtasks to make
++++++++++ timeout bound loss, not scope
++++++++++MIME-Version: 1.0
++++++++++Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
++++++++++Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit
++++++++++
++++++++++Tangle subtasks previously ran for up to 600s total elapsed and then
++++++++++got SIGKILL'd; the entire run was lost because providers (Codex
++++++++++especially) tend to draft full implementations in their response
++++++++++stream and apply_patch only at the very end. A timeout mid-generation
++++++++++discarded everything.
++++++++++
++++++++++This commit changes the timeout from 'budget for the entire task' to
++++++++++'budget for not making progress', and structures the subtask itself so
++++++++++progress is materialized as incremental file edits with explicit
++++++++++checkpoint markers.
++++++++++
++++++++++Three coordinated changes:
++++++++++
++++++++++1. **Checkpoint protocol header** prepended to each tangle subtask
++++++++++   prompt. The model is required to work in micro-steps: one
++++++++++   apply_patch per micro-step, followed by '### CHECKPOINT: <desc>'
++++++++++   on its own line. Includes a worked example and an explanation of
++++++++++   why (the orchestrator is checkpoint-aware).
++++++++++
++++++++++2. **Checkpoint-aware wait loop** in tangle_develop. Each subtask is
++++++++++   killed when:
++++++++++     - It produces no first checkpoint in OCTOPUS_TANGLE_FIRST_CHECKPOINT_TIMEOUT
++++++++++       seconds (default 240, accommodates repo exploration), OR
++++++++++     - It idles OCTOPUS_TANGLE_IDLE_TIMEOUT seconds between
++++++++++       checkpoints (default 120), OR
++++++++++     - Total elapsed exceeds OCTOPUS_TANGLE_HARD_CEILING (default 1800,
++++++++++       safety backstop against runaway checkpoint emission).
++++++++++   The legacy OCTOPUS_TANGLE_DEADLINE env var is honored as the hard
++++++++++   ceiling for backward compatibility.
++++++++++
++++++++++3. **Resume-on-timeout** for subtasks killed with completed
++++++++++   checkpoints. The orchestrator re-spawns the same provider with a
++++++++++   RESUME header listing the completed checkpoints; the model picks
++++++++++   up from where it left off. Bounded by OCTOPUS_TANGLE_MAX_RESUMES
++++++++++   (default 2) and OCTOPUS_TANGLE_RESUME_CEILING (default 900s).
++++++++++
++++++++++Plus:
++++++++++- New helper scripts/helpers/checkpoint-counter.sh — scans a
++++++++++  subtask's result file for '### CHECKPOINT:' markers and writes a
++++++++++  state file whose mtime advances only when a new checkpoint lands.
++++++++++  The wait loop polls this mtime to determine idle time.
++++++++++- _tangle_kill_subtask helper extracted from the old kill code path.
++++++++++
++++++++++Toggle the whole thing off with OCTOPUS_TANGLE_CHECKPOINTS=false
++++++++++(falls back to legacy total-elapsed behavior).
++++++++++
++++++++++Addresses the symptom seen in v9.38.0-lestephen.6 PR-2 tangle:
++++++++++both Codex subtasks ran 600s, generated substantial draft code in
